{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNHJXTqJhre36LqKj9RS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WVpdnwVajuxjGLJDqka56o","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-claude-repair2-_t2diw0q/deployment/claude/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-release-install/SKILL.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1922,"cache_read_input_tokens":31996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1922},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f43aa78-a75d-4a83-a00a-f53a718022d2","uuid":"7aecf9d4-e955-4a63-bef2-3beb1e95e45a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:56:14.837Z","request_id":"req_011CgNHJXDh4adp24noDhc14","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WVpdnwVajuxjGLJDqka56o":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-claude-repair2-_t2diw0q/deployment/claude/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-release-install/SKILL.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WVpdnwVajuxjGLJDqka56o","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tname: stdo-release-install\n3\tdescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs release preparation or installation lifecycle management — binding an exact candidate to release conditions without inferring publication authority, and installing, updating, or removing a skill package in a disposable host workspace. Covers tenant realization and maintenance. Not for unrelated tasks.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# STDO release preparation, install, update, remove\n7\t\n8\tUse this skill to prepare a reviewable release and to manage the installation\n9\tlifecycle of this skill package in a host workspace.\n10\t\n11\t## Prepare a release (SK-10, Q11)\n12\t\n13\tBind the exact selected candidate, the release conditions, the publication grant,\n14\tand the destination, using the supported release tools. You can prepare a\n15\treviewable release **without** inferring publication authority:\n16\t\n17\t- If a local artifact grant is present but no remote publication grant is, prepare\n18\t  the exact reviewable candidate and name the destination; do **not** publish and\n19\t  do **not** invent a second final cut.\n20\t- Preserve the method's immutable-cut semantics; an implementation defect does not\n21\t  authorize editing a selected methodology.\n22\t\n23\t## Install / update / remove (SK-10, SK-11, Q12)\n24\t\n25\tInstall the complete five-skill bundle, including every resource below its five\n26\tdirectories. The entry and delegation paths require sibling skills. Claude Code\n27\tdiscovers these directories under `<workspace>/.claude/skills/`; a single directory\n28\tis not a supported independent installation.\n29\t\n30\tUse the delivered [installation helper](scripts/manage_install.py) with an exact\n31\tsource package and a selected existing workspace. For initial install:\n32\t\n33\t```\n34\tpython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py install --package <selected-package> --workspace <workspace>\n35\t```\n36\t\n37\tThe helper validates the source package and refuses any ownership receipt or\n38\tsame-name directory collision. Retain the returned receipt SHA256 and verify\n39\tactual host discovery/invocation separately. The receipt records the source\n40\tinventory and exact installed file/directory population and contents.\n41\t\n42\tFor update/removal, select the previously recorded receipt SHA256:\n43\t\n44\t```\n45\tpython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py update --package <new-package> --workspace <workspace> --receipt-sha256 <previous-receipt-sha256>\n46\tpython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py remove --workspace <workspace> --receipt-sha256 <current-receipt-sha256>\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tThe receipt must identify this bundle; every owned installed file and directory\n50\tmust still match. Local additions, modified/missing files, foreign same-name\n51\tinstallations and symlinks cause refusal before mutation. Preserve them and\n52\treconcile ownership; do not refresh a hash or delete a directory to bypass the\n53\trefusal. Unrelated siblings/configuration remain untouched. Update validates the\n54\tentire new bundle first and returns a successor receipt. There is no force or\n55\tindividual-skill update.\n56\t\n57\tUse exclusive workspace access. A filesystem error may leave partial effects;\n58\tretain the current tree/receipt and reconcile before retry. The helper reports\n59\t`effect_uncertain` rather than claiming rollback. Use disposable workspaces for\n60\ttrials; package verification is distinct from host qualification and acceptance.\n61\t\n62\t## Maintenance and bindings (SK-11)\n63\t\n64\tRead the delivered [maintenance coordinates](references/maintenance.md) for the\n65\tselected method/tool/host basis and algorithm bindings. a_c contracts are consumed,\n66\tnot reimplemented. When host behavior, tool contracts, method adoption or package\n67\tbytes change, identify affected tests and claims; do not reset unrelated valid\n68\tevidence. Required delivered links are checked against the complete bundle;\n69\tmethod and engagement Product sources remain explicit external dependencies.\n70\t\n71\t## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n72\t\n73\tWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `RELEASE.md` and `IDENTITY.md`\n74\tfor release identity and consumer adoption; `PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md` sections 2, 4,\n75\t7, 9, 12 for installed basis; `SPEC_METHOD.md` sections 2, 10, 11 and\n76\t`DESIGN_MODULE.md` for realization binding.\n77\t\n78\t## Scope and limits\n79\t\n80\tPreparing a release is not publishing one, and installing into a disposable\n81\tworkspace is not Product acceptance. This candidate performs neither publication\n82\tnor acceptance.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3f43aa78-a75d-4a83-a00a-f53a718022d2","uuid":"a9f2943c-7d23-4634-8544-5033e9dcfcfe","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:56:14.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/stdo-skills-claude-repair2-_t2diw0q/deployment/claude/workspace/.claude/skills/stdo-release-install/SKILL.md","content":"---\nname: stdo-release-install\ndescription: Use when governed STDO work in this repository needs release preparation or installation lifecycle management — binding an exact candidate to release conditions without inferring publication authority, and installing, updating, or removing a skill package in a disposable host workspace. Covers tenant realization and maintenance. Not for unrelated tasks.\n---\n\n# STDO release preparation, install, update, remove\n\nUse this skill to prepare a reviewable release and to manage the installation\nlifecycle of this skill package in a host workspace.\n\n## Prepare a release (SK-10, Q11)\n\nBind the exact selected candidate, the release conditions, the publication grant,\nand the destination, using the supported release tools. You can prepare a\nreviewable release **without** inferring publication authority:\n\n- If a local artifact grant is present but no remote publication grant is, prepare\n  the exact reviewable candidate and name the destination; do **not** publish and\n  do **not** invent a second final cut.\n- Preserve the method's immutable-cut semantics; an implementation defect does not\n  authorize editing a selected methodology.\n\n## Install / update / remove (SK-10, SK-11, Q12)\n\nInstall the complete five-skill bundle, including every resource below its five\ndirectories. The entry and delegation paths require sibling skills. Claude Code\ndiscovers these directories under `<workspace>/.claude/skills/`; a single directory\nis not a supported independent installation.\n\nUse the delivered [installation helper](scripts/manage_install.py) with an exact\nsource package and a selected existing workspace. For initial install:\n\n```\npython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py install --package <selected-package> --workspace <workspace>\n```\n\nThe helper validates the source package and refuses any ownership receipt or\nsame-name directory collision. Retain the returned receipt SHA256 and verify\nactual host discovery/invocation separately. The receipt records the source\ninventory and exact installed file/directory population and contents.\n\nFor update/removal, select the previously recorded receipt SHA256:\n\n```\npython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py update --package <new-package> --workspace <workspace> --receipt-sha256 <previous-receipt-sha256>\npython3 -I -B <this-skill-directory>/scripts/manage_install.py remove --workspace <workspace> --receipt-sha256 <current-receipt-sha256>\n```\n\nThe receipt must identify this bundle; every owned installed file and directory\nmust still match. Local additions, modified/missing files, foreign same-name\ninstallations and symlinks cause refusal before mutation. Preserve them and\nreconcile ownership; do not refresh a hash or delete a directory to bypass the\nrefusal. Unrelated siblings/configuration remain untouched. Update validates the\nentire new bundle first and returns a successor receipt. There is no force or\nindividual-skill update.\n\nUse exclusive workspace access. A filesystem error may leave partial effects;\nretain the current tree/receipt and reconcile before retry. The helper reports\n`effect_uncertain` rather than claiming rollback. Use disposable workspaces for\ntrials; package verification is distinct from host qualification and acceptance.\n\n## Maintenance and bindings (SK-11)\n\nRead the delivered [maintenance coordinates](references/maintenance.md) for the\nselected method/tool/host basis and algorithm bindings. a_c contracts are consumed,\nnot reimplemented. When host behavior, tool contracts, method adoption or package\nbytes change, identify affected tests and claims; do not reset unrelated valid\nevidence. Required delivered links are checked against the complete bundle;\nmethod and engagement Product sources remain explicit external dependencies.\n\n## Method sources (cited, not reproduced)\n\nWithin `stdo://releases/v3.0.1-rc.1/standards/`: `RELEASE.md` and `IDENTITY.md`\nfor release identity and consumer adoption; `PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md` sections 2, 4,\n7, 9, 12 for installed basis; `SPEC_METHOD.md` sections 2, 10, 11 and\n`DESIGN_MODULE.md` for realization binding.\n\n## Scope and limits\n\nPreparing a release is not publishing one, and installing into a disposable\nworkspace is not Product acceptance. This candidate performs neither publication\nnor acceptance.\n","numLines":83,"startLine":1,"totalLines":83}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WVpdnwVajuxjGLJDqka56o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
